Reinforcing: Ps,info=((T-D)/W)*V,Info: T↑ → V↑ → more agents → faster decide → T↑.
Balancing: D=D,rebuild+D,token_burn+D,alloc+D,search+D,verify; W↑ → Ps↓.
Cache: Hash(u)=H(Type||Path||Content||Sum Children); K_manifest=H(relpath||ast_hash); Delta_path!=0 → eta 0.998→0 → tau_build eta*hit+(1-eta)*compile → seconds.
Team: D,search=κ*M*K*logN; 12 repos multiply K.
Invariants Delta_path=0: Merkle keys, LLM KV-prefix, Landauer arenas, substratum stability (gov not trigger engine rebuild). Violation via symlinks/std alias already.

## 5. Blue Ocean — Unique

Do not just merge 12→3. Capability-Sealed Microkernel: repos as 14-token cspace, compiler microkernel, std servers, verify_all monitor. Sovereign LSP: ooda.ebnf → generate grammar deterministically, editors speak LSP stdio only. Merkle Registry: key=H(ast_hash||cap_set||wasm_bytes), O(log M) P2P verify. Sparing Ingress: enforce ooda outline 1.3% ρ≥0.987, forbid raw read >256 lines.

## 6. REDTEAM 4-Gate Veto

Red1 Hunter: Fake decoupling — vscode/tree-sitter JS regex vs EBNF, c_emit python re.sub _pad heuristic, hyg drift line-count snapshot. Veto conditional.
Red2 Falsifier: Repo count 0 or 50, path traversal ../, token limit 1000 vs 1048576, 256 ceiling. Veto open (2 blockers: rebuild-blocker).
Red3 Tracer: ((void)0) in registry — 100+ ooda_aero_* dummy pkgs not wired via cli/cmd_pm → chs_rt_fetch verify. Veto advisory.
Red4 Jailor: 14 CUT ambient paths; install.sh shell cannot carry &FsWriteCap, registry fetch via HttpCap, editor JS exfil. Veto partial — hybrid shell wrapper → ooda/install/install.oo with caps required.

Overall: CONDITIONAL VETO — 3-tier DAG principled, Delta_path=0 correct, 4 hubs dominate, but pure rebuild gates red (c_emit_olist guard + seed rebootstrap needed).

## 7. Proposals — Elegant 3 Options

Proposal A Minimal Closed 3-Tier RECOMMENDED: 3 repos openOODA (gov+research), ooda (engine+std+tools+qa), github.io (portal+registry+brand+dist→Releases). C=3 (-95.5%), eta 0.998, 0 redundant closures. Archive helloworld, install, registry, brand, research, qa, tree-sitter, vscode via subtree + symlink period.

Proposal B 4-Tier Provenance: Keep registry separate for Ed25519 signing isolation (portal fetch, not co-host). C=6 (-90.9%), security vs elegance tradeoff.

Proposal C Pragmatic 5-Repo: Keep challenges (renamed qa) external to resolve naming collision, helloworld separate forkable. C=10 (-84.8%), lowest migration risk.

Execute via Blueprint Phases 0-3: tag v2.9.1-baseline, delete shims, subtree merges, centralize product.yml to .github, enforce verify_all single command, lock Delta_path=0.

